{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_call_site_this", "label": "this is decided by the call site", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MDN: if the call is obj.f(), this refers to obj. Same function object, different this depending on the receiver. Nothing travels when extracted."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_method_borrowing", "label": "Method borrowing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assigning bird.sayHi = car.sayHi and calling it gives this === bird. A feature of the same rule that makes extracting a method dangerous."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_this_substitution", "label": "Sloppy-mode this substitution", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In non-strict mode undefined/null this is replaced with globalThis. Writes silently create globals. Strict (modules, classes) throws TypeError instead."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_four_detach_paths", "label": "Four ways a method loses this", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Assign to a variable; pass as a callback; destructure it out; re-attach to a different object. Callbacks are the most common form."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_thisarg", "label": "thisArg on iteration methods", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "forEach, map, filter, some, every, find, findIndex, flatMap take optional thisArg. reduce, reduceRight and sort do not. Arrows sidestep it."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_class_field_this", "label": "this in a class field initialiser", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Already bound \u2014 to the instance for an instance field, to the class for a static one. Why an arrow field captures the instance permanently."}, {"id": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_page", "label": "07.1 \u00b7 How a method loses this", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/javascript/pages/phase-4-objects-and-classes/07-this-in-methods/01-how-methods-lose-this.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lose_this_page", "target": "docs_javascript_pages_phase_4_objects_and_classes_07_this_in_methods_01_how_methods_lo